{
  "summary": "Removes the `noexcept` specifier from `LogOversizedDbCache` so exceptions thrown during configuration parsing can propagate to the outer `AppInit` handler. This allows the node to exit cleanly with an error message instead of aborting via `std::terminate` when `settings.json` contains an invalid `-dbcache` value. A test case is added to `feature_settings.py` to verify graceful failure.",
  "problem": "When `settings.json` contains a malformed or out-of-range number for `dbcache` (such as a floating-point value like `4096.5`), `GetIntArg` throws a `std::runtime_error`. Because `LogOversizedDbCache` is marked `noexcept`, this exception causes `std::terminate` to immediately abort `bitcoind` during startup rather than failing gracefully.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description reproduces the startup crash: `libc++abi: terminating due to uncaught exception of type std::runtime_error: JSON integer out of range`"
  ],
